      {
        "id": "lem-twisted-fox-jacobian-is-cellular-boundary",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "deps": [
          "def-knot-twisted-chain-complex-and-reidemeister-torsion",
          "def-knot-wada-quotient-for-deficiency-one-presentation",
          "def-group-presentation",
          "def-free-group",
          "def-group-ring",
          "thm-group-ring-is-a-unital-algebra-with-basis-g",
          "def-axiom-of-choice"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "dependency_level": 6,
        "statement": "Let $X$ be the based presentation $2$-complex with one vertex, oriented $1$-cells $x_1,\\ldots,x_n$, and oriented $2$-cells attached along words $r_1,\\ldots,r_m$ in the free group $F_n$. Let $G=\\langle x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\mid r_1,\\ldots,r_m\\rangle$ be its presented fundamental group, let $\\rho:G\\to\\mathrm{GL}_d(\\mathbb F)$ be a representation, and let $\\psi:G\\to H$ be the declared free-abelian deck map. For $\\Phi:\\mathbb F[F_n]\\to M_d(Q)$ induced by $x_j\\mapsto\\rho(x_j)\\psi(x_j)$, the twisted differential $\\partial_1$ has blocks $\\rho(x_j)\\psi(x_j)-I_d$, and the $i$th block row of $\\partial_2$ is\n\n$$\\left(\\Phi\\left(\\frac{\\partial r_i}{\\partial x_1}\\right),\\ldots,\\Phi\\left(\\frac{\\partial r_i}{\\partial x_n}\\right)\\right),$$\n\nwhere coefficient vectors are written as rows and differentials act on the right: the matrix of $\\partial_1$ is the stacked column of blocks $\\rho(x_j)\\psi(x_j)-I_d$, while the matrix of $\\partial_2$ is the $md$-by-$nd$ block matrix whose $i$th row is the displayed Fox row. The Fox derivatives use the product and inverse recursions in the Wada definition. Thus the evaluated Fox-Jacobian blocks are exactly the cellular boundary blocks of the based twisted complex of this presentation $2$-complex."
      },
